{"name":"Keepsake","hex":"#c0ced6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"keepsake","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An object given by a person and retained in memory of something or someone; something kept for sentimental or nostalgic reasons.","Specifically, a type of literary album popular in the nineteenth-century, containing scraps of poetry and prose, and engravings."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/keepsake"}],"entries":[{"title":"Souvenir","blocks":[{"text":"A souvenir, memento, keepsake, or token of remembrance is an object a person acquires for the memories the owner associates with it. A souvenir can be any object that can be collected or purchased and transported home by the traveler as a memento of a visit. The object itself may have intrinsic value, or be a symbol of experience. Without the owner's input, the symbolic meaning is lost and cannot be articulated."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Souvenir","wikidata":"Q212469"},{"title":"Gift book","blocks":[{"text":"Gift books, literary annuals, or keepsakes were 19th-century books, often lavishly decorated, which collected essays, short fiction, and poetry. They were primarily published in the autumn, in time for the holiday season and were intended to be given away rather than read by the purchaser. They were often printed with the date of the coming new year, but copyrighted with the actual year of publication."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Libertybell-cover.jpg/330px-Libertybell-cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gift_book","wikidata":"Q3975991"},{"title":"Keepsake (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Keepsake was an American emo/screamo band formed in 1997 by Paul Geller, Mark Silva and Duane Hosein in Coral Springs, Florida. Hosein joined the band An Acre Lost and ultimately had to quit Keepsake. He was replaced by Shane Halpern, former vocalist of An Acre Lost. After releasing three albums and EP on the independent label, Eulogy Recordings and Fearless Records, Geller left the band for personal reasons. He also produced three records for RED Music-distributed Undecided Records artists Shindig, Hearts Over Rome and Cru Jones. Geller moved into digital music and worked as EVP of Information Products at Grooveshark."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Keepsake_(band)","wikidata":"Q6383282"},{"title":"Keepsake (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Keepsake is a third person point-and-click adventure game developed by Canadian company Wicked Studios for Linux, Mac OS X and Windows platforms. The player plays as the main character Lydia. The quest starts that Lydia investigates what happened to Dragonvale Academy as she was on her way to meet a friend there, as she arrived she noticed that the academy was deserted. Although the game was met with mixed reviews, the developers endeavour to improve the game by releasing patches."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/92/Keepsake_Coverart.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Keepsake_(video_game)","wikidata":"Q1112638"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Haunzenbergers%C3%B6ll_1900.JPG/500px-Haunzenbergers%C3%B6ll_1900.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Haunzenbergers%C3%B6ll_1900.JPG/500px-Haunzenbergers%C3%B6ll_1900.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Souvenir porcelain mug from Germany, c. 1900","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHaunzenbergers%C3%B6ll_1900.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Souvenirloeffel.jpg/500px-Souvenirloeffel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, http